# Adaptive int element accepts a wider value

Verifies an `int[]` element widens beyond the declared `int64` width when the
assigned literal exceeds it, unlike a fixed-width `int64[]` element.

>>> source
let values: int[] = [1]
values[0] = 999999999999999999999999999999
print(values[0])

<<< stdout
999999999999999999999999999999

<<< stderr
